# NestJS bootstrap that creates the app but never registers helmet / security
# headers. block-absence: find the bootstrap block, flag it when no helmet/
# useSecurityHeaders call appears inside. Scoped to NestJS projects via requires.
# Source: docs/research/nestjs.md rows 1-2 (docs.nestjs.com/security/helmet).
id: MEST-NEST-001
title: NestJS app bootstrapped without helmet / security headers
category: security
severity: warning
engine: block-absence
action: warn
skip_comments: true
skip_strings: true
requires:
  framework: @nestjs
target:
  extensions: .ts .js
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ node_modules/ dist/ build/
patterns:
  - regex: \basync\s+function\s+bootstrap\s*\(
block_inner: (?i)helmet|useSecurityHeaders
block_trigger: NestFactory\.create
confidence: 0.6
message: "NestJS bootstrap() creates the app but never registers helmet()/useSecurityHeaders() — responses ship without CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, etc. Add app.use(helmet()) (Express) or app.register(helmet) (Fastify)."
fix: "In bootstrap(), after NestFactory.create, call app.use(helmet()) (Express) or app.useSecurityHeaders() / app.register(helmet) (Fastify)."
